# TypeScript Development Rules

## Type Safety
- Always use strict TypeScript with proper type annotations
- Define interfaces for all data structures (see [src/types/product.ts](mdc:src/types/product.ts))
- Use proper generic types for React components and hooks
- Avoid `any` type - use proper typing or `unknown` when necessary

## Component Patterns
- Use functional components with TypeScript
- Define proper prop interfaces for all components
- Use React.ComponentProps for extending HTML element props
- Implement proper event handler types

## Import/Export
- Use named exports for components and utilities
- Use default exports only for main components (App, main entry points)
- Group imports: React imports first, then third-party, then local imports
- Use path aliases: `@/` for src directory

## Code Style
- Use semicolons consistently
- Use double quotes for strings
- Use trailing commas in objects and arrays
- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Use camelCase for variables and functions
- Use PascalCase for components and interfaces

## Error Handling
- Use proper try-catch blocks for async operations
- Define custom error types when needed
- Use optional chaining and nullish coalescing
- Implement proper fallback states for loading and error conditions